2026-09-27T13:20:14.1618809Z [36;1m# A REQUIRED additional app that does not enable is an ENVIRONMENT[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1619280Z [36;1m# failure, and it must not be allowed to resurface as APPLICATION[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1621274Z [36;1m# failures. It used to: `|| echo "::warning::…, continuing"` let the[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1621768Z [36;1m# run proceed without the dependency, and the consuming app's tests[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1622177Z [36;1m# then died on the absent classes.[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1622443Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1622727Z [36;1m# Measured on ConductionNL/hermiq, full-scope run 31490144919, six[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1623328Z [36;1m# PHPUnit cells, perfect 6/6 correlation:[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1623625Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1623899Z [36;1m#   enable ok      -> Tests: 1500, Errors: 5, Failures: 1   (x3)[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1624491Z [36;1m#   enable FAILED  -> Tests: 1500, Errors: 12               (x3)[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1624927Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1625148Z [36;1m# The seven extra "errors" were `Interface[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1625693Z [36;1m# "OCA\OpenRegister\Service\Flow\IFlowNodeLogActions" not found` and[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1626296Z [36;1m# `Call to undefined method MockObject_ToolRegistryFacade::[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1626748Z [36;1m# describeTools()` — which read as app debt and were an absent app.[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1627349Z [36;1m# Two distinct causes, one deterministic (OpenRegister declares[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1627803Z [36;1m# min-version="32"; the cell was stable31) and one transient[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1628245Z [36;1m# (`curl error 60 … self-signed certificate` during composer install[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1628712Z [36;1m# left Twig missing, so enabling crashed). Both deserve a red job:[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1629179Z [36;1m# the first is a real configuration error, the second is re-runnable.[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1629822Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1630125Z [36;1m# ⚠️ The failure flag goes through a FILE, not a variable. The loop[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1630614Z [36;1m# body runs in a subshell (it is fed by a pipeline), so a variable set[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1631090Z [36;1m# inside it is invisible after `done` — the same trap the gate runner[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1631479Z [36;1m# documents at its gate-30 loop.[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1631748Z [36;1mif [ '[]' != '[]' ]; then[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1632085Z [36;1m  rm -f "${RUNNER_TEMP:-/tmp}/additional-app-enable-failed"[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1632482Z [36;1m  echo '[]' | jq -r '.[].app' | while read -r name; do[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1632809Z [36;1m    echo "Enabling app: $name"[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1633105Z [36;1m    if ! php occ app:enable "$name"; then[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1634284Z [36;1m      echo "::error::Failed to enable required additional app '$name'. This is an ENVIRONMENT failure, not an application failure — the run cannot measure this repository without it. Common causes: the app declares a min-version above the Nextcloud ref this cell tests, or its composer install did not complete."[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1635551Z [36;1m      echo "$name" >> "${RUNNER_TEMP:-/tmp}/additional-app-enable-failed"[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1635910Z [36;1m    fi[0m
2026-09-27T13:20:14.1636095Z [36;1m  done[0m
